/*1351. Count Negative Numbers in a Sorted Matrix
Leetcode Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/count-negative-numbers-in-a-sorted-matrix/?envType=daily-question&envId=2025-12-28

Approach: 

he matrix is sorted in non-increasing order both row-wise and column-wise.

So in each row, all negative numbers appear to the right.

We start from the bottom-right corner, where negatives are most likely.

For each row, we scan from right to left and count negatives.

As soon as we hit a non-negative number, we stop scanning that row (because left side will also be non-negative).

*/
/**
 * @param {number[][]} grid
 * @return {number}
 */
var countNegatives = function(grid) {
    let c=0;
    let m=grid.length;
    let n=grid[0].length;
    for(let i=m-1;i>=0;i--){
        for(let j=n-1;j>=0;j--){
            if(grid[i][j]>=0)break;
            c++;
        }
    }
    return c;
};
